[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64958,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mucinous carcinoma, intestinal type, of the vagina is a primary vaginal adenocarcinoma with features similar or identical to those seen in colorectal carcinomas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64959,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8480/3 Mucinous adenocarcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64960,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C71.0 &amp; XH1S75 Adenocarcinoma of vagina &amp; Mucinous adenocarcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64961,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> cloacogenic adenocarcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64962,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64963,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most commonly lower vagina, especially posteriorly</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64964,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours occur across a wide age range but usually in older women; in the largest study to date, the women were aged 36&ndash;86&nbsp;years (median: 56&nbsp;years) {24722061}. Most patients present with vaginal bleeding or a mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64965,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No epidemiological data are available.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64966,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "<p>The etiology is unknown. Some cases arise in association with intestinal-type adenomas and/or benign-appearing intestinal-type epithelium, suggesting an adenoma&ndash;carcinoma sequence {24722061}. Some tumours arise in or near the Bartholin gland duct. Identical vulvar tumours occur just outside the vaginal introitus and are probably closely related.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-26T14:49:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64967,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64968,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours usually form a polypoid mass but are sometimes ulcerated. They are typically small (&lt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;cm) {24722061}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64969,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours display intestinal adenocarcinoma features. There is intracytoplasmic mucin, and goblet cells are frequently present; one reported tumour had prominent neuroendocrine cells {24722061}. Tumours directly extending from the gastrointestinal tract should be excluded. Intestinal-type mucinous carcinomas of the vagina typically express CDX2 and CK20 and are negative for ER, with variable CK7 staining {24722061}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64970,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Similar to colorectal adenocarcinoma, intestinal-type adenocarcinoma is characterized by crowded sheets of malignant glandular cells with enlarged vesicular nuclei, macronucleoli, and delicate cytoplasm, although these tumours are not typically diagnosed by cytological methods. The presence of intracytoplasmic mucin and goblet cells supports intestinal differentiation but is not always seen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64971,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64972,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> adenocarcinoma with intestinal differentiation.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> goblet cells are usually present but are not required.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64973,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The staging is the same as for other vaginal carcinomas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64974,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are few reported cases with long-term follow-up. Occasional recurrences and deaths have been reported {24722061}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]